{"name":"Blue Sabre","hex":"#575f6a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"sabre","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light sword with a curved blade, sharp along the front edge, part of the back edge, and at the point.","A modern fencing sword modeled after the sabre."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strike or kill with a sabre.","To open (a bottle) via sabrage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sabre"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sabre","blocks":[{"text":"A sabre or (American English) saber is a type of backsword with a curved blade associated with the light cavalry of the early modern and Napoleonic periods. Originally associated with Central European cavalry such as the hussars, the sabre became widespread in Western Europe during the Thirty Years' War. Lighter sabres also became popular with infantry of the early 17th century. In the 19th century, models with less curving blades became common and were also used by heavy cavalry."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sabre"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Rose_Contract_of_1812_Cavalry_Saber_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Rose_Contract_of_1812_Cavalry_Saber_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Rose_Contract_of_1812_Cavalry_Saber_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Rose_Contract_of_1812_Cavalry_Saber_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Rose_Contract_of_1812_Cavalry_Saber_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Rose_Contract_of_1812_Cavalry_Saber_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARose_Contract_of_1812_Cavalry_Saber_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Magyar_honfoglal%C3%A1skori_szably%C3%A1k.jpg/250px-Magyar_honfoglal%C3%A1skori_szably%C3%A1k.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Magyar_honfoglal%C3%A1skori_szably%C3%A1k.jpg/500px-Magyar_honfoglal%C3%A1skori_szably%C3%A1k.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Magyar_honfoglal%C3%A1skori_szably%C3%A1k.jpg/250px-Magyar_honfoglal%C3%A1skori_szably%C3%A1k.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikiped